## What was fixed

`DEVICE_ACCESS(lca_pci_conf)` in `src/devices/dev_lca.c` used ONE variable for two things — the
configuration CYCLE TYPE (`d->ioc_conf & 1`) and the DESTINATION BUS. A guest storing `0x1` to
IOC_CONF (a value the register's own guard ACCEPTS) then made any access in the PCI config window
reach `fatal("TODO. Non-zero bus."); exit(1)`.

The fix, in full:

```c
	type1 = d->ioc_conf & 1;	/*  #515  */
	bus = 0;			/*  #515  */

	if (!type1) {			/*  #515  */
		for (dev=0; dev<21; dev++)
			if (tag & (0x800U << dev))
				break;
		if (dev >= 21)
			dev = 0;
	} else {
		bus = (tag >> 16) & 0xff;	/*  #515  */
		dev = (tag >> 11) & 0x1f;	/*  #515  */
	}

	func = (tag >> 8) & 7;

	if (type1 && bus == 0) {		/*  #515  */
		odata = reg == 0? (uint64_t) -1 : 0;
	} else {
		bus_pci_setaddr(cpu, d->pci_data, bus, dev, func, reg);
		bus_pci_data_access(cpu, d->pci_data, writeflag == MEM_READ?
		    &odata : &idata, len, writeflag);
	}

	if (writeflag == MEM_READ)
		memory_writemax64(cpu, data, len, odata);

	return 1;
```

Decode above it: `reg = (relative_addr >> 5) & 0xfc;` and `tag = (relative_addr >> 5) & ~0xff;`.
`bus_pci_data_access` on an absent device returns all-ones at register 0 and zero elsewhere for
READS, and for WRITES prints `[ ... write to non-existant device, bus %i func %i device %i ]`.
A write to a REGISTERED device instead prints `... NOT YET SUPPORTED. bus %i, device %i, function
%i (%s) register 0x%02x`. Exactly one device is registered: `i82378zb` at bus 0, device 7, func 0.

## The 14 rows, and what each one detects

| row | what it asserts |
|---|---|
| `bus ctl` / `bus ctlsig` | LIVENESS + DEVICE SIGNATURE: a type-0 read at window+0 returns the empty-slot all-ones |
| `bus kill` / `bus attrib` | the host survives the armed access; a death must carry this arm's own diagnostic |
| `t1 alive` | a type-1 write to a non-zero bus does not end the host |
| `t1 anchor` | that write prints exactly `bus 1 func 2 device 3 ]` — ANCHORED, absolute position |
| `t1 alias` | a type-1 write with bus 0 prints no `bus 0 func 0 device 0 ]`, checkpointed by a LATER anchor store so "never executed" cannot pass as "refused" |
| `t1 rdval` | a type-1 read at bus 0 returns `0xffffffffffffffff` — pins the refusal's synthesised VALUE |
| `t1 dev7rd` | a type-1 read at bus 0 / **dev 7** returns all-ones and NOT the real device's `0x304848086` |
| `t1 dev7wr` | a type-1 write at bus 0 / dev 7 does not print `device 7, function 0 (i82378zb)` |
| `t0 write` | a type-0 write still reaches bus_pci and prints `bus 0 func 0 device 5 ]` |
| `t0 alive` / `t0 real` / `t0 accept` | a type-0 read of dev 7 still returns exactly `0x304848086` |

