Best coverage gap: type‑1, bus‑0 refusal reads at nonzero registers.

Nothing pins the returned value when reg ranges from 0x04 through 0xfc, in steps of four. This gap already exists with len held at eight bytes and func held at zero. **No row constrains it.** Both t1 rdval and t1 dev7rd constrain the refusal’s all-ones result at register zero; every other row also uses register zero.

The specified result throughout this nonzero-register cell is zero. That is an entire outcome of the refusal logic that the suite never exercises. Killing M2_nullval demonstrates sensitivity to the register-zero result; it establishes nothing about the required zero result elsewhere.

I rank this above the func and len gaps because it identifies an explicit, wholly untested branch while retaining the suite’s existing function and access width. The supplied fix implements that branch correctly, but the 14 rows do not establish its correctness.
